Gentoo: use a system Crubit (cc_bindings_from_rs) with a system Rust toolchain.

Since M153-M156 several default-on features (Blink's FontFormatCheck, the Web
Bundle parser in //components/web_package, ...) are written in Rust and called
from C++ only through Crubit-generated bindings (`cpp_api_from_rust`); there is
no C++ fallback.  Upstream only enables `cpp_api_from_rust` with its own
toolchain (third_party/rust-toolchain, which ships cc_bindings_from_rs) and a
stdlib built from source, whose core/alloc/std bindings come from
//build/rust/std/rules.

This adds the GN arg `rust_crubit_root` (e.g. /usr/lib/crubit/<rust slot>,
installed by dev-util/crubit, built against the very same rustc as
`rust_sysroot_absolute`).  When it is set:

* `enable_cpp_api_from_rust` is true for target toolchains (not for the
  `*_for_rust_host_build_tools` toolchains, as upstream);
* cc_bindings_from_rs and Crubit's GN support library come from
  `rust_crubit_root` (same layout as Chromium's toolchain package), rustfmt
  from `rust_sysroot`, and the optional `rust_crubit_clang_format` replaces
  the bundled buildtools/linux64-format/clang-format (formatting only);
* the C++ bindings of the prebuilt stdlib (rs_core.h/rs_alloc.h/rs_std.h, same
  paths/namespaces/metadata as upstream's) are generated by running
  cc_bindings_from_rs in .rmeta mode over the stdlib of `rust_sysroot`
  (//build/rust/std/prebuilt_std_bindings.{gni,py}).

With `rust_crubit_root` unset nothing changes.

Rebased for 157: the executable paths now live in
build/rust/gni_impl/crubit_shared_args.gni (shared by cpp_api_from_rust.gni and
rust_api_from_cpp.gni), so cc_bindings_from_rs and the clang-format override are
set there instead of in cpp_api_from_rust.gni.

